window.docContents[100].resolve({"/Overview/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Overview--Simple-check-sat":{"contents":"The result of a check-sat is either sat, unsat, or unknown. The Solver.checkSat function\ntakes a optional continuation for each; the defaults report the result as unexpected.\n\n#eval Env.runIO do\n  let (solver, b1, i1) ← setup\n  println! \"check-sat\"\n  for f in ← solver.getAssertions do println! \"∧ {f}\"\n  solver.checkSat\n    (ifSat := do\n      println! \"→ sat\"\n      -- notice `b1`'s type is lean's `Bool`\n      let b1Val ← solver.getValue b1\n      -- notice `i1`'s type is lean's `Int`\n      let i1Val ← solver.getValue i1\n      println! \"  values : b1 ↦ {b1Val}, i1 ↦ {i1Val}\"\n      -- alternatively you can ask for value as `Term _`\n      let b1ValTerm ← solver.getValueTerm b1\n      let i1ValTerm ← solver.getValueTerm i1\n      println!\n        \"  terms  : b1 ↦ {b1ValTerm}, i1 ↦ {i1ValTerm}\")\n\n\ncheck-sat\n∧ (or (not b1) (and b1 (< 0 i1)))\n→ sat\n  values : b1 ↦ false, i1 ↦ 0\n  terms  : b1 ↦ false, i1 ↦ 0\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API\u0009Overview","header":"1.2. Simple check-sat","id":"/Overview/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Overview--Simple-check-sat"}});